{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PRC-OAVS Room Pressurization - Application 6763 (Floating Dampers, AOV or Floating Reheat, Optional Perimeter Radiation)",
  "model_slug": "prc-oavs-6763-floating-damper-reheat-perimeter-radiation",
  "short_model": "PRC-OAVS Floating Damper 6763",
  "aliases": [
    "Application 6763",
    "App 6763",
    "570-810P",
    "PRC-OAVS",
    "Siemens Pressurized Room Controller",
    "Siemens lab room pressurization"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Laboratory room airflow and pressure controller",
  "applies_to": "Pressurized laboratory rooms with one supply terminal (with reheat) and one general exhaust terminal on floating damper actuators, with optional discharge control and perimeter radiation, on the Siemens BACnet PRC-OAVS controller 570-810P with offboard air modules 550-819B.",
  "summary": "Application 6763 holds a set airflow offset between supply and general exhaust to pressurize a lab room, and also handles ventilation and room temperature, on a Siemens BACnet PRC-OAVS controller over BACnet MS/TP. Both dampers use floating actuators. Reheat can be driven 0-10 V or floating, and three heating modes are available: reheat from the room loop, reheat from a discharge loop, or discharge loop plus a 0-10 V perimeter radiation valve. Two offset setpoints (PRS1/PRS2) can be switched, and the room can be run without a supply box or without an exhaust box.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "VOL DIFFRNC = (GEX VOL + OTHER EXH) - (SUP VOL + OTHER SUP); it is positive in a negatively pressurized room.",
    "Control priority when functions conflict: pressurization first, then ventilation, then temperature.",
    "OTHER SUP and OTHER EXH (AO 61, AO 89) hold airflows the controller does not measure (snorkels, canopies, other boxes); keep them current for correct pressurization.",
    "ALARM ENA (AO 122) adds values to pick which alarms drive ALARM DO7; NET ALM CMD (BO 23) always drives it."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PRC-OAVS with Slow Floating Damper Control, AOV or Floating Reheat, Optional Discharge Control and Optional AOV Perimeter Radiation, Application 6763, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1059",
    "revision_date": "2014-10-15",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/v73Q6Z9Hc6wkGE1u6jCRpQ/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk and calibrate the airflow modules. The BMS commands day/night with DAY.NGT (BO 29), sets the day setpoints and the airflow offset, keeps OTHER SUP / OTHER EXH current where unmeasured airflows exist, and reads room temperature, supply and exhaust airflow, the airflow difference and the ventilation and pressurization alarms.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 88",
        "name": "VOL DIF STPT",
        "why": "Exhaust-minus-supply airflow offset, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "SUP VOL",
        "why": "Measured supply airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 30",
        "name": "GEX VOL",
        "why": "Measured general exhaust airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 62",
        "name": "VOL DIFFRNC",
        "why": "Exhaust minus supply airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 22",
        "name": "VOL DIF ALM",
        "why": "Room pressurization (offset) alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 68",
        "name": "VENT ALM",
        "why": "Ventilation alarm"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Day/night is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES the switch sets it; on a network the field panel or BMS commands it. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary override from the room unit button. PRESS STATE (BI 51) picks which offset setpoint (PRS1DIF or PRS2DIF STPT) is active.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "OTHER SUP (AO 61) and OTHER EXH (AO 89) take airflows from equipment not wired to this controller; the guide suggests updating them over the network (PPCL) when they change. NET ALM CMD (BO 23) lets the field panel switch the local alarm output.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the point table lists its factory value as 99.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6765, although the document is for 6763.",
      "Duct areas (SUPDUCT AREA, GEXDUCT AREA) and flow coefficients must match the installed boxes before airflow readings are valid."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "VOL DIFFRNC and VOL DIF STPT are positive for a negative (exhausting) room.",
      "In supply-tracks-exhaust mode the supply flow is capped by HTG FLO MAX in heating; setting it equal to HTG FLO MIN may be too tight to hold pressure (the guide suggests FLOW START = FLOW END instead).",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and calibration settings are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely."
    ]
  },
